# Config File for the Benachmarking
# I created this so we have a centralized, easy to change place to store the configuraion of the Benachmarking
# benchmarks/parse_benchconfig.py has the parsing code so have look for details
# In short: the ":" symbol is used to separate key and value. Put "layer: yourlayername" on some line. All following lines (also in : separated key value pairs)
# should contain the config if some config item like here versions or B is a list as value just use space separation
# Probably the best way is to have a look at the groupnorm example below

layer: groupnorm
    versions: baseline invertdiag
    B: 2 4 6 8 10 12
    C: 4
    D: 3
    num_groups: 2
    I: 4

